The numbers is a list of 3, 4, 2.
The last is the last position of numbers.
The largest is 0.
For every spot from 0 to last.
If item spot of numbers is more than largest, set largest to item spot of numbers.

The counts is a list of largest plus 1 zeros.
For every spot from 0 to last.
The value is item spot of numbers.
Set item value of counts to item value of counts plus 1.

The best is a list of largest plus 1 zeros.
For every value from 1 to largest.
The skip is 0.
If value is more than 1, set skip to item (value minus 1) of best.
The take is value times item value of counts.
If value is more than 1, set take to take plus item (value minus 2) of best.
If skip is more than take, set item value of best to skip, otherwise set item value of best to take.

Show item largest of best.
